%% references.bib — MSc thesis, Biswajeet Panda
%%
%% ===========================================================================
%% HOUSE STYLE (applied consistently to every entry below)
%% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
%% Rendering is Cranfield Numbered (biblatex style=numeric-comp, sorting=none),
%% so entries appear in order of first citation. To keep the printed reference
%% list uniform, every entry follows the same rules:
%%
%%  1. ENTRY TYPE follows the *publication venue*, not the file format:
%%       @inproceedings  peer-reviewed conference paper (CoRL, RSS, ICRA, IROS,
%%                       NeurIPS, ICLR, ICML, CVPR, AISTATS)
%%       @article        peer-reviewed journal paper (T-RO, RA-L, IJRR, PNAS,
%%                       Nature Mach. Intell., JASA)
%%       @misc           preprint with no peer-reviewed venue, software,
%%                       model checkpoint, or technical report
%%       @thesis         student dissertation (with an explicit `type` field)
%%
%%  2. AUTHORS are given in full "Surname, Forename" form. Where the author list
%%     is a very large collaboration, it is truncated with `and others`, which
%%     biblatex renders as "et al." — this is used sparingly and only for
%%     collaborations, never to shorten a list of four or five named authors.
%%
%%  3. VENUE NAMES are given in full with the community acronym in parentheses,
%%     e.g. "Conference on Robot Learning (CoRL)". Ordinal numbers ("7th") and
%%     locations are omitted throughout so that every venue reads the same way.
%%
%%  4. arXiv IDENTIFIERS appear ONLY on preprint-only entries (@misc), and use
%%     the biblatex-native fields `eprint`, `eprinttype` and `eprintclass`. They
%%     are NEVER placed in a `journal` field, which would make a preprint render
%%     as though it were a journal article. A paper that has since appeared at a
%%     peer-reviewed venue is cited by that venue alone, so that published and
%%     unpublished sources are visibly distinguished in the reference list.
%%
%%  5. `note` carries bibliographic information only (edition, erratum, "Model
%%     checkpoint: ..."). Author affiliations are NOT recorded — they are not
%%     part of a reference and previously made the list read inconsistently.
%%
%%  6. SOFTWARE and MODELS use @misc with `howpublished` set to one of
%%     {Software}, {Model checkpoint} or {Technical report}, plus `url` and
%%     `urldate`.
%%
%%  7. TITLE CASE is preserved by brace-protecting proper nouns and system
%%     names only, e.g. {{RT-2}}, {{MuJoCo}}, {{SmolVLA}}.
%%
%%  8. PAGE RANGES are given for journal articles and for conference papers with
%%     stable pagination. Proceedings published through PMLR (CoRL, AISTATS,
%%     ICML) and open-review venues (ICLR, RSS) are cited without pages, as is
%%     conventional for those series.
%%
%% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
%% BEFORE SUBMISSION: verify each entry against the publisher record (venue,
%% year, page range, DOI). DOIs have deliberately not been guessed; add them
%% from the publisher page if the programme handbook requires them.
%% ===========================================================================


